  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Samoa-Australia Police Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SAPP leads and coordinates AFP engagement with the Samoa Police, Prisons and Corrections Service (SPPCS). The SAPP provides the framework for collaboration between the SPPCS and AFP. The SAPP 2021-25 design came into effect July 2021 and is framed by the following Partnership Goal: to support SPPCS to maintain a safe and stable Samoa. Two Partnership Outcomes support this goal: SPPCS leadership use executive management skills and strengthened policy and planning frameworks to guide the organisation; and SPPCS has enhanced capability and standardisation in key areas aligned to both SPPCS and AFP policy and planning frameworks.</narrative>
  </description>
